 v4.4.beta4.official [93d270693]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta4 - Fedora Linux 41 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 560 Series (radeonsi, polaris11, LLVM 19.1.0, DRM 3.60, 6.12.15-200.fc41.x86_64) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-2500K CPU @ 3.30GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nAt certain emission rates (`3` and `6`, at least), GPU particles appear to emit at a rate of 1 instead of the configured emission amount.\n\nThe `GPUParticles3D` instances in the MRP and the following video are lined up with incrementing emission values, from 1 to 6. Observe that emission values of 1, 3, and 6 emit at the same rate.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/41d56cdb-447d-441e-85d1-c1505eae47b5\n\n#### Related\n\nNew pull request:\n\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103121\n\nRelated:\n\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83699\n\nOld issues:\n\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/68809\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/80863\n\nOld pull requests:\n\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/81913\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/81902\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Load `test_scene_1.tscn` of the attached project in a current master build (4.4-beta4, as of writing).\n2. Observe that the GPU particle instances that are set to emission amounts `3` and `6` are emitting at the same rate as the instance set to an emission amount of `1`. It's possible that results vary here based on GPU.\n3. Load the project in a build of Godot that includes this PR's changes.\n4. Observe that each GPU particle in the sequence emits 1 more than the previous, as expected from their configured emission amounts.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[godot-4_4-gpu-particle-scale-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18904604/godot-4_4-gpu-particle-scale-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_i